{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453344-building-gadget-based-talents","id":1453344,"title":"Building gadget based Talents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-24T04:22:14-07:00","id":1453344,"title":"Building gadget based Talents","content":"I picked up Aberrant. I love the system so far. One thing I'm struggling with is the idea of Talents in a game of Aberrant. If I'm making someone like the Punisher or Nick Fury, I can understand these characters. They have a lot of skill and grit.<br /> <br /> What if I want to replicate Hawkeye's trick arrows or Bat Man's utility belt? Is there a way to replicate these variable powers as a Talent without jumping up to Nova Q-tech?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26906-jeffreybezos","name":"JeffreyBezos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T04:33:16-07:00","id":1453345,"title":"","content":"The arent going to be as powerful, period. Pick up that gift in aberrant and accept it. You even have a higher target number on dice. <br /> <br /> Inspired Tech is a thing though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T05:34:38-07:00","id":1453350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JeffreyBezos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453344-building-gadget-based-talents#post1453344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I picked up Aberrant. I love the system so far. One thing I'm struggling with is the idea of Talents in a game of Aberrant. If I'm making someone like the Punisher or Nick Fury, I can understand these characters. They have a lot of skill and grit.<br /> <br /> What if I want to replicate Hawkeye's trick arrows or Bat Man's utility belt? Is there a way to replicate these variable powers as a Talent without jumping up to Nova Q-tech?</div> </div> </div> </div>You want the Well-Equipped Edge from page 97 of Aberrant (RAW this requires being a member of the Directive, which fits Fury, but not Batman. Storyguide permission could let another Path justify it. Personally if you\u2019ve invested in some super science related Gifts, I\u2019d let any Talent take it and narratively justify it as a gadget they had prepped as long as it\u2019s within the power ranged of Inspired tech).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-24-2021, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T05:41:14-07:00","id":1453351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453344-building-gadget-based-talents?p=1453345#post1453345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The arent going to be as powerful, period. Pick up that gift in aberrant and accept it. You even have a higher target number on dice.<br /> <br /> Inspired Tech is a thing though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> .... the OP didn't ask about being as powerful?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T05:52:25-07:00","id":1453352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453344-building-gadget-based-talents?p=1453345#post1453345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The arent going to be as powerful, period. Pick up that gift in aberrant and accept it. You even have a higher target number on dice. <br /> <br /> Inspired Tech is a thing though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed; including Inspired Tech that replicates the effects of Gifts. The core book describes one that operates as a \u201cfreeze ray\u201d, if I recall correctly. <br /> <br /> Also bear in mind that your gadgets can access Scale that you can't. A mechanical exoskeleton can operate on a higher Might Scale thank a human can; a jet pack (a la the Rocketeer) can grant you the equivalent of flight and of some speed Scale. <br /> <br /> Trick arrows and utility belt gadgets are child's play for Inspired Super-Science; and coupled with The Bigger They Are (the Gift introduced in TC:Ab) \u2014 which, I remind you, can be incorporated into suitable Inspired gadgets that can't justify having large Scale themselves but <i>can</i> justify being unusually effective against high-Scale Novas \u2014 you can have an Inspired gadgeteer who is surprisingly effective against Novas. <br /> <br /> Also, you should be able to use your Inspiration to [I[retroactively[/I] craft just what you need for a given situation: if you have access to the TC:A! Kickstarter manuscript, look over the special kind of Dramatic Editing that mesmerists get. I could see creating a Gift (\u201cI Have Just the Thing\u201d or \u201cThe Right Tool for the Job\u201d) that lets a Talent access those rules, but for their Inspired Tech rather than their own Gifts: spend the requisite Inspiration, and for one scene you get to replace one of the pieces of Inspired Tech that you normally carry around with you with an alternate design that's more suitable to the situation you find yourself in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-24-2021, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T05:55:57-07:00","id":1453353,"title":"","content":"Many Batman/James Bond style gadgets could just be esoteric mundane technology, so they get that stuff through their Paths. Then you just need an appropriate Skill Trick or Gift to pull out the right one at need. After all, the Hidden Advantage Gift already lets you pull a weapon out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> Maybe make a Gift like - A number of times per session equal to your X Facet, you can spend a point of Inspiration to access a hand-held non-weapon piece of mundane gear appropriate to your needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T05:57:24-07:00","id":1453354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453344-building-gadget-based-talents?p=1453352#post1453352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, you should be able to use your Inspiration to [I[retroactively[/I] craft just what you need for a given situation: if you have access to the TC:A! Kickstarter manuscript, look over the special kind of Dramatic Editing that mesmerists get. I could see creating a Gift (\u201cI Have Just the Thing\u201d or \u201cThe Right Tool for the Job\u201d) that lets a Talent access those rules, but for their Inspired Tech rather than their own Gifts: spend the requisite Inspiration, and for one scene you get to replace one of the pieces of Inspired Tech that you normally carry around with you with an alternate design that's more suitable to the situation you find yourself in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that's reinventing the wheel given the Well-Equipped Edge already exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T06:13:37-07:00","id":1453355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453344-building-gadget-based-talents?p=1453354#post1453354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> I feel like that's reinventing the wheel given the Well-Equipped Edge already exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to review that when I have the time. But I think that there may be room for Inspiration to enhance what Well Equipped does.<br /> <br /> EDIT: okay; I've reviewed it, and you're right. I think my own house rule will be that <i>any</i> Edge that \u201cmakes Dramatic Editing available in a limited form, but using Momentum instead of Inspiration\u201d should be available to any Talent with an appropriate concept regardless of the normal prerequisites. (Or, more simply, available to any Talent, since \u201cwith an appropriate concept\u201d is a given for <i>every</i> trait that ends up on the character sheet.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-24-2021, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T06:57:17-07:00","id":1453357,"title":"","content":"Also: TC:Ab's \u201ccore tech\u201d parallels the core book's advanced Super-Science, and TC:Ab's Nova Tech parallels the core book's Inspired Super-Science. The mechanics aren't precisely the same (nova-tech doesn't let you incorporate Gifts into your design, for example); but they should be close enough that most of the new rules for Super-Science in TC:Ab should be applicable to the Super-Science that Talents use: \u201cWell-Equipped\u201d talks about being able to do this with core tech and Nova-tech, so a Talent should be able to do it with Advanced and Inspired Super-Science. And the reverse engineering rules let you eventually turn Nova-tech into core-tech; in the same way, a Talent should be able to reverse-engineer her Inspired Super-Science to produce an equivalent Advanced Super-Science. And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T09:34:52-07:00","id":1453374,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies everyone! <br /> <br /> When I picked up Trinity Continuum, I fell in love with the rules, the art, the setting, everything. I was actually worried a bit about having a community around it. It's so awesome to see active community involvement.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of playing with scale and maybe even just handwaving some of it to paths like you could with other equipment. I think here's how I'm going to rule it in my game. I do like the idea of well-equipped for the once off specialist problem solving equipment that Batman or Black Widow might have. The device that hacks into the mainframe. The rebreather that allows you to dive under water. The micro torch that lets you cut through the steel door.<br /> <br /> I would worry about more variable combat equipment, the trick arrows, smoke bombs and batarangs. From a rules, and possibly even balance point of view, I can see the idea of spending inspiration to pull out a specific piece of equipment once per encounter working. On a more practical side? Where's the fun in that? Whipping out sonic arrows one round, then a cable arrow to zip down and drop kick bad guy #7 is just good fun times. I'm going to roll with, paths and a grab bag of goodies for variable combat bombs and arrows, then the well-equipped edge for the more unique problem solving gadgets.<br /> <br /> Thanks everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26906-jeffreybezos","name":"JeffreyBezos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T10:15:43-07:00","id":1453376,"title":"","content":"Hawkeye is easy. You get a Bow with the Variable Ammo Tag on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":786,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","user":"thedonnie","date":". 06-24-2021, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T12:48:07-07:00","id":1453393,"title":"","content":"If you really want to play Batman, you may also want to look into buying multiple one or two point instances of the Artifact Powered Edge for extraordinary equipment you carry all the time; things like his grapple launcher or body armor. You could even use the Armory Enhanced Edge to whip up counters to specific situations between sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T13:33:54-07:00","id":1453400,"title":"","content":"Artifact would be good to get for things that you would use often. Going back to the Batman example, the Batmobile and the Batcomputer might be good to get with Artifact. The minor stuff like the various things in the utility belt might be emulated using the Armory Enhanced Edge. Just declare what you want to use and design them on the fly with the SG. Also, bear in mind that you could use Batarangs with the Variable Ammo tag on them and buy that with Artifact Edge as well.<br /> It is not that hard to make a Batman or a Hawkeye or Moon Knight using the Core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T13:41:23-07:00","id":1453401,"title":"","content":"The Wealth edge and the corresponding Powered Edge also provide a lot of advanced equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}